            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fas is a cell surface death receptor critical for immune regulation. In this issue of Immunity, Butt et al. (2015) show that Fas eliminates B cells that have become uncoupled from positive and negative selection in the germinal center.</AbstractText>
